  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 108 AM CDT Sun Sep 13 2026\n\nSurface boundary is currently situated right along, or just\nsouth, of the KS/OK border. How this boundary meanders back\nnorthward into this afternoon will determine how hot the area \ncan get. Given max temperature uncertainty and front placement, \nhave knocked down temperatures a few touches from the NBM \noutput. A few solutions like MET remain too cold, and MAV is \nbetter but still may be a touch too low. As the previous \nforecaster noted, NBM is probably running too hot with northward\nextent. To compromise, maintained upper 90s to near 100 in \nsouthern counties, but decreased them northward from there. \nTemperatures may still be overdone in some spots, but generally \nlike where the forecast is at for now.\n\nVery little doubt on the heat's extent into Monday as the front\nmoves northward and clears the area. Widespread upper 90s to \naround 100 looks probable across the entire CWA. These\ntemperatures are near record highs for September 14th. Gusty\nwinds will also be in the forecast Monday afternoon with a stiff\ndownslope flow from the southwest. Winds will be be 25-35 \nsustained, with higher gusts.\n\nStorm chances are minimal across the forecast area today with\nPOPs around 20% or less at best. The boundary could serve as a\nfocus for a storm or two, but coverage is not expected to be\nsignificant and any storms that do develop will lose steam very\nquickly after dark. With the exception of steep low-level lapse\nrates, not much going for anything severe with much lower shear\nthan yesterday. Gusty winds would be the risk should a storm or\ntwo develop. The next significant chance of rain will be Monday\nand into next week when a strong shortwave traverses into the\nPlains and brings another cold front. Scattered thunderstorms\nwould be expected in this regime, with likely to definite POPs \n60-80% Monday-Wednesday. Strong storms and heavy rainfall could\nbe associated with the activity, but day to day details will be\nironed out as we get closer.",
